{"nodes": [{"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "label": "Framework-comparison benchmarks", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Answers \"how do you compare to X?\" with a number instead of an adjective (#27); a separate tree because putting third-party code on the other side of the table changes what fair has to mean."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_separate_manifest", "label": "Own dependency manifest for benchmark targets", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeps the shipped closure at two runtime dependencies, keeps lint:audit meaningful (advisories in a benchmark target are not advisories in actor-ts), and keeps bun run bench runnable on a clean clone."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_typecheck_compare", "label": "typecheck:compare", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only check that covers this tree; without it nothing would, which is how ten benchmark suites sat broken on a removed export for months (#506)."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "label": "The fairness contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A comparison benchmark is easy to run and hard to believe; a result that breaks one of the seven rules is a bug, not a finding."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_completion_verified", "label": "Completion-verified measurement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fairness rule 1: every arm asserts the system actually processed the operations and writes both counts; the last published figure was ~10x too high because the mailbox dropped 90% of a synchronous enqueue while the harness counted the batch it asked for (#1027, #972)."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_one_workload", "label": "One workload, one set of constants", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fairness rule 2: a constant that drifts in one runner turns the whole table into fiction while every individual row still looks plausible, so the report generator cross-checks and fails on divergence."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_logging_off", "label": "Logging off in every arm", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fairness rule 3: an arm that writes log lines is measuring its logger."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_one_framework_per_subprocess", "label": "One framework per subprocess", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fairness rule 4: module-level state, JIT profiles and GC pressure must not cross arms."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_one_runtime_named", "label": "One runtime, named (Bun)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fairness rule 5, and a limitation rather than a preference: the shared harness pulls in src/ for highResNow, whose .js suffixes and two enums Node's strip-only TypeScript mode cannot load, so running the neighbours on Node would mean not running them through the same harness."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_semantic_mismatch_labelled", "label": "Semantic mismatches labelled, never silently mapped", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fairness rule 6: where a framework has no equivalent the arm records a skip with a reason; where the nearest thing is used the note travels with the row into RESULTS.md and every published table."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_cross_language_separation", "label": "Same-runtime and cross-language never share a table", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fairness rule 7: two JavaScript frameworks on one machine through one harness is a measurement; a framework on another virtual machine through a mirrored harness is a different kind of claim, and mixing them into one ranking hides that."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_actor_ts", "label": "actor-ts arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_nact", "label": "nact arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The closest neighbour: same model, same runtime, functional API; it creates actors synchronously where actor-ts defers construction to a dispatcher turn."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_xstate", "label": "XState v5 arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Included for reach though it is a statechart library; it processes events synchronously and has no request/response primitive, so its ask row is send + waitFor on a snapshot."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_akka_java", "label": "Akka (JVM, Java) arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_akka_scala", "label": "Akka (JVM, Scala 3) arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The binding question: the same framework at the same version through its native-language API, so any gap against the Java arm reads as the binding."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_pekko_java", "label": "Pekko (JVM, Java) arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pinned to 1.6.0, the newest stable release: publishing against the 2.0.0-M3 milestone would measure a released framework against an unreleased one."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_pekko_scala", "label": "Pekko (JVM, Scala 3) arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The fourth corner of the 2x2: down a column is the licence question, across a row the binding one."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_akka_net", "label": "Akka.NET arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A third runtime for the same design, which is what makes the runtime's own contribution visible; uses the classic actor API its documentation leads with."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_orleans", "label": "Orleans virtual-actor arm", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The one genuinely different model: grains activate on first call, there is no caller-visible create or stop, and a grain call is an RPC, so three of its four rows measure a near-equivalent and say so."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_mill", "label": "Mill as the single JVM build tool", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three build tools across four cross-language arms was a variable with nothing to do with what is measured; the launcher is committed as scripts only (mill, mill.bat) and downloads itself, and Windows needs the .bat because the POSIX script refuses to run off Linux/macOS."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_mill_version_pin", "label": ".mill-version and pinned JDK", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The launcher scripts fall back to a nightly development build, so a tree without the pin would silently build with whatever that happens to be; the JDK is provisioned through coursier so two machines measure on the same build."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_forked_process_effect", "label": "Forked clean JVM versus warm build-tool host", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The old Maven goal ran the benchmark inside Maven's own warm JVM; forking a clean process costs the alternating-volley row roughly a third to a half, so the earlier JVM volley numbers were flattered by a harness artefact and removing it is a correction, not a regression."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_akka_licence", "label": "Akka 2.8.8 under BUSL-1.1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Benchmarking falls under the non-production grant, and the licence is carried into every published table next to the number because a reader comparing frameworks is usually also choosing one."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_repo_akka_io_403", "label": "repo.akka.io answers 403 anonymously", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Releases from 2.9 onwards publish only there, and a benchmark nobody else can reproduce is not evidence, so the arm stays on the newest publicly resolvable artifact and says so."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_hand_mirrored_harness", "label": "Hand-mirrored harness instead of JMH", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JMH is the better microbenchmark tool but measures differently (forked JVMs, blackholes, its own warmup); a comparison whose two sides use different methodologies cannot be read as one table, so the JVM side reproduces the JavaScript protocol down to the percentile rule."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_idiomatic_scala", "label": "Idiomatic functional Scala arms", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "State advances by returning a new behavior rather than mutating a field, because measuring what people actually write is the point of the arm; the cost (a behavior and closure per message) is disclosed on the three rows it can move, and the sending side is kept byte-identical to the Java arms so the pair differs in one thing only."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_jvm_ask_thread_parking", "label": "JVM ask row measures thread parking, not messaging", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Driving the system from a non-actor thread parks and unparks on a CompletableFuture; the .NET arms await instead and land ~5x higher on the same row while the JVM arms lead the tell rows, so the row is the cost of asking from outside the actor system on that runtime."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_removed_no_framework_floor", "label": "Removed: the no-framework floor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A column two to three orders of magnitude above the rest read as \"the frameworks are wasteful\" when a direct call does none of the work, and it was also the least trustworthy figure in the suite (16% between consecutive runs); a comparison should help someone choose between the options in front of them."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_rejected_comedy", "label": "Evaluated and rejected: comedy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It declares @types/node 10.3.3 as a runtime dependency, shadowing the real one so every node:-prefixed import in src/ stops type-checking, and brings core-js@2 with a lifecycle script; the measurement is not the reason it is absent, the cost to the tree is."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_workload_constants", "label": "js/workload.ts shared workload constants", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Batch sizes and iteration counts live here once and are mirrored as literals with a pointer back in the cross-language runners."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_interleaved_rounds", "label": "Interleaved rounds with published spread", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Round 1 of every arm then round 2, so machine noise lands on every arm; the mean uses all rounds where a median would report one and discard the rest, and the spread is published so a row whose rounds disagreed is visible as that. Across five single rounds the ask rate varied 2%, 15% and 34% on three arms while their ordering never changed."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_missing_toolchain_skip", "label": "A missing toolchain is skipped, not failed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RESULTS.md carries a date and commit per arm, so a partial run leaves untouched arms visibly attributed to the run that measured them; skipped arms are listed on the success path too, because a partial run reported as a plain green tick is how a release publishes figures for arms that never ran. A failed arm no longer discards the run either (#1326)."}, {"id": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_launcher_mode", "label": "Committed 100755 mode on the Mill launchers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A launcher present but not executable is a broken checkout, not a missing toolchain; the mode is asserted against the git index because the working tree cannot answer the question on Windows, which is why the JVM arms were unrunnable on Linux for as long as they were (#1325)."}], "edges": [{"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_completion_verified", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_one_workload", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_logging_off", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_one_framework_per_subprocess", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_one_runtime_named", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_semantic_mismatch_labelled", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_fairness_contract", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_cross_language_separation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_separate_manifest", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_separate_manifest", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_typecheck_compare", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_actor_ts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_nact", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_xstate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_akka_java", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_akka_scala", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_pekko_java", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_pekko_scala", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_framework_comparison", "target": "benchmarks_comparison_readme_arm_akka_net", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/comparison/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight"